(5751294, 835447, 23484, '<td valign="top">Hey Terry, your shot just sucks! So there. Actually, I really like it. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would have probably given this a 7.  It is a tad dark but I don''t look at that as a bad thing. I generally like those darker, spookier shots.  I like it.</td>', 'Hey Terry, your shot just sucks! So there. Actually, I really like it. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would have probably given this a 7.  It is a tad dark but I don''t look at that as a bad thing. I generally like those darker, spookier shots.  I like it.', '2009-12-02 20:14:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751456, 835487, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AbeSapien2:</b></div><hr/><i> A white church, the quintessential symbol of organised Religion with the shadow of the older Tree of Life, indicative of quite another and older Celtic Natural religion, towering over it is a telling juxtaposition and a statement with much more between the lines than would first appear in a casual look at this. A favourite in this challenge to me - The chimney and the structure bear many straight lines, the Tree is curved and bends with the changing winds. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>many thanks for taking the time for your comments here.</td>', 'Originally posted by AbeSapien2: A white church, the quintessential symbol of organised Religion with the shadow of the older Tree of Life, indicative of quite another and older Celtic Natural religion, towering over it is a telling juxtaposition and a statement with much more between the lines than would first appear in a casual look at this. A favourite in this challenge to me - The chimney and the structure bear many straight lines, the Tree is curved and bends with the changing winds.   many thanks for taking the time for your comments here.', '2009-12-02 21:55:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751513, 835501, 61315, '<td valign="top">I thought this was yours Penny! ;-) Nice shot of the cathedral.</td>', 'I thought this was yours Penny! ;-) Nice shot of the cathedral.', '2009-12-02 22:26:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751584, 834614, 50695, '<td valign="top">only top 10 I gave a 7 to. Nice shot.</td>', 'only top 10 I gave a 7 to. Nice shot.', '2009-12-02 23:39:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751585, 835254, 50695, '<td valign="top">I knew this was you, and I knew you''ve done naughty nuns before, but I just couldn''t resist one nun making heavy metal devil horns and the other giving me the finger while smiling sweetly. 7 from me.</td>', 'I knew this was you, and I knew you''ve done naughty nuns before, but I just couldn''t resist one nun making heavy metal devil horns and the other giving me the finger while smiling sweetly. 7 from me.', '2009-12-02 23:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751588, 835489, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Lighting is pretty good but could be better (get that Timfy guy to give you lessons) and it seems you tried to pull a bit out of the darker side to the point of getting a bit of noise/grain.  I will say I don''t get the title.  I know you''re not, but it almost seems as though you''re implying you''d be better than Christ to sacrifice for mankind''s sins or some such. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t recognize you, Doc!<br/> <br/>He''s saying that he should have died for his own sins, not mankind''s sins. The other side of that coin is Christ''s amazing act of Mercy, ignoring what "should" be and granting Doc eternal life.<br/> <br/>Next religion challenge I''m going to put on a robe and sit under a tree, smiling. "It should have been me."</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Lighting is pretty good but could be better (get that Timfy guy to give you lessons) and it seems you tried to pull a bit out of the darker side to the point of getting a bit of noise/grain.  I will say I don''t get the title.  I know you''re not, but it almost seems as though you''re implying you''d be better than Christ to sacrifice for mankind''s sins or some such.   I didn''t recognize you, Doc! He''s saying that he should have died for his own sins, not mankind''s sins. The other side of that coin is Christ''s amazing act of Mercy, ignoring what "should" be and granting Doc eternal life. Next religion challenge I''m going to put on a robe and sit under a tree, smiling. "It should have been me."', '2009-12-02 23:45:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5751591, 835507, 50695, '<td valign="top">only 2 10s for dashboard Jesus?? What''s wrong with people? And one of them was me!</td>', 'only 2 10s for dashboard Jesus?? What''s wrong with people? And one of them was me!', '2009-12-02 23:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
